  "title": "Ryan Serhant: How to Get People to Say Yes",
  "summary": "Ryan Serhant is a real estate broker, founder of SERHANT., and star of Bravo’s Million Dollar Listing New York and Netflix’s Owning Manhattan. He explains how to sell without making people feel sold to: build a connection, help first, and earn the right to ask. He also breaks down the psychology of attention and persuasion, … The post Ryan Serhant: How to G…",
  "content": "<p>Ryan Serhant is a real estate broker, founder of SERHANT., and star of Bravo’s <em>Million Dollar Listing New York</em> and Netflix’s <em>Owning Manhattan</em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<div>\n            <div>\n            <div>\n                <div>\n                                            <div>\n                            <div></div>\n                        </div>\n                                        \n                </div>\n                <div></div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    \n            \n        <div>\n        <h3>Featured clips</h3>\n        <div>\n                                            <div>\n                    <div>\n                                                    <img width=\"300\" height=\"164\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screenshot-2026-10-13-at-8.08.44-AM-300x164.png\" alt=\"The 1,000 Minutes a Day Framework\">                                                                            <div>\n                                \n                                12:28                            </div>\n                                            </div>\n                                            <p>The 1,000 Minutes a Day Framework</p>\n                                    </div>\n                                                <div>\n                    <div>\n                                                    <img width=\"300\" height=\"165\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screenshot-2026-10-13-at-8.07.59-AM-300x165.png\" alt=\"The 3Fs to Land Your Follow-Up\">                                                                            <div>\n                                \n                                20:57                            </div>\n                                            </div>\n                                            <p>The 3Fs to Land Your Follow-Up</p>\n                                    </div>\n                                                <div>\n                    <div>\n                                                    <img width=\"300\" height=\"156\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screenshot-2026-10-13-at-8.05.41-AM-300x156.png\" alt=\"How to Handle Ego in Negotiations\">                                                                            <div>\n                                \n                                31:21                            </div>\n                                            </div>\n                                            <p>How to Handle Ego in Negotiations</p>\n                                    </div>\n                                                <div>\n                    <div>\n                                                    <img width=\"300\" height=\"162\" src=\"https://fs.blog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Screenshot-2026-10-13-at-8.06.20-AM-300x162.png\" alt=\"The Personal Cost of Success\">                                                                            <div>\n                                \n                                46:51                            </div>\n                                            </div>\n                                            <p>The Personal Cost of Success</p>\n                                    </div>\n                            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n\n\n<p>He explains how to sell without making people feel sold to: build a connection, help first, and earn the right to ask. He also breaks down the psychology of attention and persuasion, showing how to get people’s attention, hold it, and turn it into business.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>We explore why he rejects “fake it till you make it,” how he approached his Million Dollar Listing audition as the person he wanted to become, and why ego gets in the way of closing deals.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Ryan explains his time management framework of treating each day as a bank of 1,000 minutes changed the way he works, and why success can still feel insufficient after you achieve all of your dreams. </p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Available Now: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xr7tUPuc7xA\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">YouTube</a> | <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/5oNTyQ8FR9XH8LHZB8kzSi?si=F4NGn06LTcGTbg0rEwuLBQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Spotify</a> | <a href=\"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/how-to-get-people-to-say-yes-ryan-serhant/id990149481?i=1000796113104\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apple Podcasts</a> | <a href=\"https://fs.blog/knowledge-project-podcast-transcripts/ryan-serhant/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Transcript</a></strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p><em>+ <a href=\"https://fs.blog/membership/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Members</a> get the longer, extended version of this conversation, with additional content not included in the public release.<br></em></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://fs.blog/knowledge-project-podcast/ryan-serhant/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ryan Serhant: How to Get People to Say Yes</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://fs.blog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Farnam Street</a>.</p>",
